:"த்தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"contesting"},{"surface":"போகிய","parts":[{"text":"போகு","lemma":"போகு","gloss":"go"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"which went"}],"gloss":"which has ceased"},{"surface":"சிலை","parts":[{"text":"சிலை","lemma":"சிலை","gloss":"bow"}],"gloss":"bow"},{"surface":"தார்","parts":[{"text":"தார்","lemma":"தார்","gloss":"garland"}],"gloss":"garland"},{"surface":"மார்ப","parts":[{"text":"மார்ப","lemma":"மார்பு","gloss":"O one with the chest"}],"gloss":"O one with the chest"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செய்து","parts":[{"text":"செய்","lemma":"செய்","gloss":"do"},{"text":"து","lemma":"து","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having done"},{"surface":"இரங்கா","parts":[{"text":"இரங்கு","lemma":"இரங்கு","gloss":"regret"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without regretting"},{"surface":"வினை","parts":[{"text":"வினை","lemma":"வினை","gloss":"deeds"}],"gloss":"deeds"},{"surface":"சேண்","parts":[{"text":"சேண்","lemma":"சேண்","gloss":"distance"}],"gloss":"far"},{"surface":"விளங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"விளங்கு","lemma":"விளங்கு","gloss":"shine"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"புகழ்","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்","lemma":"புகழ்","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெய்தரும்","parts":[{"text":"நெய்","lemma":"நெய்","gloss":"ghee/fat"},{"text":"தரும்","lemma":"தரு","gloss":"giving"}],"gloss":"ghee-giving"},{"surface":"கானல்","parts":[{"text":"கானல்","lemma":"கானல்","gloss":"coastal grove"}],"gloss":"coastal grove"},{"surface":"நெடியோய்","parts":[{"text":"நெடியோய்","lemma":"நெடியோய்","gloss":"O great one"}],"gloss":"O great one","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எய்த","parts":[{"text":"எய்து","lemma":"எய்து","gloss":"reach"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitival suffix"}],"gloss":"to reach"},{"surface":"வந்தனம்","parts":[{"text":"வந்தனம்","lemma":"வா","gloss":"we came"}],"gloss":"we came"},{"surface":"யாம்","parts":[{"text":"யாம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"we"}],"gloss":"we"},{"surface":"ஏத்துகம்","parts":[{"text":"ஏத்து","lemma":"ஏத்து","gloss":"praise"},{"text":"கம்","lemma":"கம்","gloss":"we shall"}],"gloss":"we shall praise"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Those who worship, well you know indeed / others' blame those who speak, their words you do not believe indeed / you yourself saw evil if you see / fittingly having investigated, in that manner you punish / having come, feet having approached, before you if they stand / punishment also you mitigate, you, more than before indeed / nectar cooked, unceasing fragrant seasoned food / to those who come, without limiting, blameless life / women contesting except, warriors / contesting gone, bow-garlanded-chested one! / having done, not regretting deeds, far-shining fame / ghee-giving grove great one! / to reach we came, we, we shall praise many indeed","translation":"You know well those who worship you. You do not believe the words of those who slander others. If you see an evil that you yourself have witnessed, you investigate it fairly and punish accordingly. But if they come, bow at your feet, and stand before you, you mitigate their punishment, showing even greater mercy than before. Yours is a blameless life of giving food cooked like nectar with unceasing fragrant seasoning to all who come, without limit. O warrior with a chest adorned with garlands and a bow, where only women contest with you in love, and no enemy warriors dare to fight! O tall lord of the ghee-yielding coastal groves, whose fame shines far for deeds done without regret! We have come to reach you, and we shall sing your many praises!","modern":"உன்னை வணங்குபவர்களை நீ நன்றாக அறிவாய். பிறரைப் பழித்துக் கூறுவோரின் சொற்களை நீ நம்ப மாட்டாய். நீயே நேரில் கண்ட தீமையைக் கண்டால், அதனை ஆராய்ந்து அதற்குத் தகுந்தவாறு தண்டிப்பாய். ஆனால், அவர்கள் உன்னிடம் வந்து, உன் அடிகளைப் பணிந்து, உனக்கு முன்னால் நின்றால், உனது தண்டனையைக் குறைத்து முன்னைவிடப் பெரிதும் அருள் செய்வாய். அமிழ்தம் போன்ற, நறுமணமுள்ள தாளித்த உணவை வருவோர்க்கு எல்லையின்றி வழங்கும் பழிப்பில்லாத வாழ்க்கை உன்னுடையது. மகளிர் உன்னோடு ஊடல் கொள்வதே அன்றி, வீரர்கள் உன்னோடு போர் செய்ய அஞ்சி ஓடிய, வில்லேந்திய மார்பை உடையவனே! செய்த பின் வருந்தாத செயல்களால் எங்கும் விளங்கும் புகழையும், நெய் வளம் தரும் கடற்கரைச் சோலைகளையும் உடைய நெடியோனே! உன்னை அடைந்து நாங்கள் உன்னைப் பலவாறாகப் புகழ்ந்து பாடுவோம்.","explanation":"The poet Ūṉ Poti Pasuṅ Kuṭaiyār sings in praise of the Chola king Neytalaṅ Kāṉal Iḷañcēṭ Ceṉṉi. He extols the king's virtues of justice, mercy, and generosity. The king is described as one who discerns true loyalty, ignores slander, and punishes wrongdoers justly, yet forgives those who surrender. His court is famous for boundless hospitality, serving delicious, fragrant food to all visitors. The poet uses a beautiful contrast: the only 'war' or contest the king faces is the playful lovers' quarrels (mountain-like chest contested by women), as no male warriors dare to oppose his bow. The poem belongs to the pāṭāṇ tiṇai, which focuses on praising a king's strength, generosity, and righteous rule.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}